            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## Meso 0.3.3

- Keyboards and mice on a 2.4 GHz receiver are found again, and their shortcuts work.
- Smooth scrolling, scroll direction, speed and tilt settings apply to mice again.
- Add Device shows a receiver nothing has been heard through yet, and finds its mouse when you move it.
- Keyboards follow the mouse to the computer that has it, not the next channel.
- Meso says when a keyboard leaves, a controller arrives, or key and pointer handling stops. Each notice has its own switch in Settings › Devices and starts off; cable alerts now live there too.
- Granting Input Monitoring after launch takes effect without restarting.
- Seven crashes fixed in Meso, Studio, Notes and the CLI.
- Shelf edits, note drafts, clipboard originals, plugin updates and settings survive interruptions and failed writes.
- Wording polished in all five languages.
]]></description>
