        <item>
            <title>0.3.1</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:48:42 +0800</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/linmi/meso/releases</link>
            <sparkle:minimumUpdateVersion>1154</sparkle:minimumUpdateVersion>
            <sparkle:version>11509</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.3.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## Meso 0.3.1

**New**
- USB drives get a page of their own: real capacity, what's on the drive and what changed last, how it's connected, its reading and writing, its history, and erasing it for the Mac or PC it's for.
- Queue for Pasting: a window that lines up what you copy and pastes it in order; drag rows to reorder them.
- Shelf: drop files on AirDrop or Compress, and drop pictures to make them smaller.
- Screenshots' History shows your pictures and films.
- Translate shows the text and its translation side by side, keeps as many translations as you choose, and exports its history as CSV.

**Better**
- Quick Notes opens in front, ready to write in; a recording's window opens in front, and stopping takes it out of the menu bar at once.
- The menu bar panel's quick actions show their names, grouped by category.
- Logitech mice show their own picture and button marks.
- On Home, a display or drive sits on the side of the Mac it's plugged into, and a Studio Display looks like one.
- Floating cards can be resized from their edges and corners. When something fails, the card says why in your language, with a feedback button beside close.
- Films with clicks are written in half the time.
- Meso does less while idle: it no longer polls for audio, reads macOS's log less often, and the Time page shows today first.
- Wording reviewed throughout, in all five languages.
]]></description>
